{"data":[{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.1802.05751","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.1802.05751","identifiers":[{"identifier":"1802.05751","identifierType":"arXiv"}],"creators":[{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Niki","familyName":"Parmar","name":"Parmar, Niki","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Ashish","familyName":"Vaswani","name":"Vaswani, Ashish","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Jakob","familyName":"Uszkoreit","name":"Uszkoreit, Jakob","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Łukasz","familyName":"Kaiser","name":"Kaiser, Łukasz","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Noam","familyName":"Shazeer","name":"Shazeer, Noam","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Alexander","familyName":"Ku","name":"Ku, Alexander","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Dustin","familyName":"Tran","name":"Tran, Dustin","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]}],"titles":[{"title":"Image Transformer"}],"publisher":"arXiv","container":{},"publicationYear":2018,"subjects":[{"subject":"Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV)","lang":"en","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"FOS: Computer and information sciences","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"},{"schemeUri":"http://www.oecd.org/science/inno/38235147.pdf","subject":"FOS: Computer and information sciences","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2018-02-15T20:37:15Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2018-02-19T01:01:11Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2018-02-19T18:44:17Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v2"},{"date":"2018-02-20T01:17:40Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v2"},{"date":"2018-06-15T23:27:07Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v3"},{"date":"2018-06-19T00:03:14Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v3"},{"date":"2018-02","dateType":"Available","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2018","dateType":"Issued"}],"language":null,"types":{"schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint","citeproc":"article","bibtex":"misc","ris":"GEN","resourceType":"Article"},"relatedIdentifiers":[],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"3","rightsList":[{"rightsUri":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/","rights":"arXiv.org perpetual, non-exclusive license"}],"descriptions":[{"descriptionType":"Abstract","description":"Image generation has been successfully cast as an autoregressive sequence generation or transformation problem. Recent work has shown that self-attention is an effective way of modeling textual sequences. In this work, we generalize a recently proposed model architecture based on self-attention, the Transformer, to a sequence modeling formulation of image generation with a tractable likelihood. By restricting the self-attention mechanism to attend to local neighborhoods we significantly increase the size of images the model can process in practice, despite maintaining significantly larger receptive fields per layer than typical convolutional neural networks. While conceptually simple, our generative models significantly outperform the current state of the art in image generation on ImageNet, improving the best published negative log-likelihood on ImageNet from 3.83 to 3.77. We also present results on image super-resolution with a large magnification ratio, applying an encoder-decoder configuration of our architecture. In a human evaluation study, we find that images generated by our super-resolution model fool human observers three times more often than the previous state of the art."},{"descriptionType":"Other","description":"Appears in International Conference on Machine Learning, 2018. Code available at https://github.com/tensorflow/tensor2tensor"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.05751","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":0,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"mds","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"downloadCount":0,"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":0,"created":"2022-03-03T00:26:12Z","registered":"2022-03-03T00:26:12Z","published":null,"updated":"2022-03-03T00:26:12Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"arxiv.content","type":"clients"}}}},{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.1809.04281","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.1809.04281","identifiers":[{"identifier":"1809.04281","identifierType":"arXiv"}],"creators":[{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Cheng-Zhi Anna","familyName":"Huang","name":"Huang, Cheng-Zhi Anna","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Ashish","familyName":"Vaswani","name":"Vaswani, Ashish","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Jakob","familyName":"Uszkoreit","name":"Uszkoreit, Jakob","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Noam","familyName":"Shazeer","name":"Shazeer, Noam","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Ian","familyName":"Simon","name":"Simon, Ian","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Curtis","familyName":"Hawthorne","name":"Hawthorne, Curtis","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Andrew M.","familyName":"Dai","name":"Dai, Andrew M.","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Matthew D.","familyName":"Hoffman","name":"Hoffman, Matthew D.","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Monica","familyName":"Dinculescu","name":"Dinculescu, Monica","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Douglas","familyName":"Eck","name":"Eck, Douglas","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]}],"titles":[{"title":"Music Transformer"}],"publisher":"arXiv","container":{},"publicationYear":2018,"subjects":[{"subject":"Machine Learning (cs.LG)","lang":"en","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"Sound (cs.SD)","lang":"en","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"Audio and Speech Processing (eess.AS)","lang":"en","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"Machine Learning (stat.ML)","lang":"en","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"FOS: Computer and information sciences","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"},{"schemeUri":"http://www.oecd.org/science/inno/38235147.pdf","subject":"FOS: Computer and information sciences","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"},{"subject":"FOS: Electrical engineering, electronic engineering, information engineering","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"},{"schemeUri":"http://www.oecd.org/science/inno/38235147.pdf","subject":"FOS: Electrical engineering, electronic engineering, information engineering","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2018-09-12T07:15:26Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2018-09-13T00:07:49Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2018-10-10T20:23:04Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v2"},{"date":"2018-10-12T00:02:48Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v2"},{"date":"2018-12-12T07:42:08Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v3"},{"date":"2018-12-13T01:07:03Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v3"},{"date":"2018-09","dateType":"Available","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2018","dateType":"Issued"}],"language":null,"types":{"schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint","citeproc":"article","bibtex":"misc","ris":"GEN","resourceType":"Article"},"relatedIdentifiers":[],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"3","rightsList":[{"rightsUri":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/","rights":"arXiv.org perpetual, non-exclusive license"}],"descriptions":[{"descriptionType":"Abstract","description":"Music relies heavily on repetition to build structure and meaning. Self-reference occurs on multiple timescales, from motifs to phrases to reusing of entire sections of music, such as in pieces with ABA structure. The Transformer (Vaswani et al., 2017), a sequence model based on self-attention, has achieved compelling results in many generation tasks that require maintaining long-range coherence. This suggests that self-attention might also be well-suited to modeling music. In musical composition and performance, however, relative timing is critically important. Existing approaches for representing relative positional information in the Transformer modulate attention based on pairwise distance (Shaw et al., 2018). This is impractical for long sequences such as musical compositions since their memory complexity for intermediate relative information is quadratic in the sequence length. We propose an algorithm that reduces their intermediate memory requirement to linear in the sequence length. This enables us to demonstrate that a Transformer with our modified relative attention mechanism can generate minute-long compositions (thousands of steps, four times the length modeled in Oore et al., 2018) with compelling structure, generate continuations that coherently elaborate on a given motif, and in a seq2seq setup generate accompaniments conditioned on melodies. We evaluate the Transformer with our relative attention mechanism on two datasets, JSB Chorales and Piano-e-Competition, and obtain state-of-the-art results on the latter."},{"descriptionType":"Other","description":"Improved skewing section and accompanying figures. Previous titles are \"An Improved Relative Self-Attention Mechanism for Transformer with Application to Music Generation\" and \"Music Transformer\""}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.04281","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":0,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"mds","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"downloadCount":0,"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":0,"created":"2022-03-02T14:46:56Z","registered":"2022-03-02T14:46:57Z","published":null,"updated":"2022-03-02T14:46:57Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"arxiv.content","type":"clients"}}}},{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.1706.06255","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.1706.06255","identifiers":[{"identifier":"1706.06255","identifierType":"arXiv"}],"creators":[{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Mohsen","familyName":"Mahoor","name":"Mahoor, Mohsen","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Alireza","familyName":"Majzoobi","name":"Majzoobi, Alireza","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Zohreh S.","familyName":"Hosseini","name":"Hosseini, Zohreh S.","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Amin","familyName":"Khodaei","name":"Khodaei, Amin","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]}],"titles":[{"title":"Leveraging Sensory Data in Estimating Transformer Lifetime"}],"publisher":"arXiv","container":{},"publicationYear":2017,"subjects":[{"subject":"Systems and Control (eess.SY)","lang":"en","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"FOS: Electrical engineering, electronic engineering, information engineering","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"},{"schemeUri":"http://www.oecd.org/science/inno/38235147.pdf","subject":"FOS: Electrical engineering, electronic engineering, information engineering","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2017-06-20T03:21:28Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2026-06-04T17:58:31Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2017-06","dateType":"Available","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2017","dateType":"Issued"}],"language":null,"types":{"schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint","citeproc":"article","bibtex":"misc","ris":"GEN","resourceType":"Article"},"relatedIdentifiers":[],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"1","rightsList":[{"rightsUri":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/","rights":"arXiv.org perpetual, non-exclusive license"}],"descriptions":[{"descriptionType":"Abstract","description":"Transformer lifetime assessments plays a vital role in reliable operation of power systems. In this paper, leveraging sensory data, an approach in estimating transformer lifetime is presented. The winding hottest-spot temperature, which is the pivotal driver that impacts transformer aging, is measured hourly via a temperature sensor, then transformer loss of life is calculated based on the IEEE Std. C57.91-2011. A Cumulative Moving Average (CMA) model is subsequently applied to the data stream of the transformer loss of life to provide hourly estimates until convergence. Numerical examples demonstrate the effectiveness of the proposed approach for the transformer lifetime estimation, and explores its efficiency and practical merits."},{"descriptionType":"Other","description":"2017 North American Power Symposium (NAPS), Morgantown, WV, 17-19 Sep. 2017"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.06255","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":1,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"mds","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"downloadCount":0,"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":0,"created":"2022-03-04T00:45:08Z","registered":"2022-03-04T00:45:10Z","published":null,"updated":"2026-06-05T05:16:58Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"arxiv.content","type":"clients"}}}}],"meta":{"total":158,"totalPages":53,"page":1},"links":{"self":"https://api.datacite.org/dois?query=%28transformer%29+AND+publicationYear%3a%5b2017+TO+2018%5d\u0026resource-type-id=preprint\u0026sort=relevance\u0026page[number]=1\u0026page[size]=3","next":"https://api.datacite.org/dois?page%5Bnumber%5D=2\u0026page%5Bsize%5D=3\u0026query=%28transformer%29+AND+publicationYear%3A%5B2017+TO+2018%5D\u0026resource-type-id=preprint"}}